Z||000000||fldevel||11-13-2001||10:39 AM||||what are some simptoms of the cat. converter going bad ?? i have hard starts and practicaly NO horsepower under 2300 RPM <BR>plus i dont know if this is the origonal cat cause it seems alot smaller than the one on my 2m4 ||||reg||1
Z||000001||88CoupeV6||11-13-2001||10:44 AM||||Usually the car will lose power at all rpm's. If you do need one, I recommend Rodney's <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rodneydickman.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierocritter||11-13-2001||10:46 AM||||Does it have a bad odor form the exhaust? Never had one go, but I here they smell bad. Another thing is low output of exhaust at the exhaust pipe!||||reg||1
Z||000003||fldevel||11-13-2001||11:08 AM||||hmm im trying to isolate the "hard starts" problem ..ive changed about every electronic doodad on the engine ..the engine has great compression i dont know what else it could be ..||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||11-13-2001||11:12 AM||||Cat's going bad sometimes smell like rotting eggs. Usually when they get red hot. Generally the car has to strain to hit higher RPM's, Car runs rich, hard starting, and/or whooshing sound when rev'd in neutral/out of gear. When car is cool, bang on the converter, If it sounds like someone put a baseball in there it's bad. Usually the cats start to clog first then the catalyst melts into a glob.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||11-13-2001||03:16 PM||||If it's the cat and you don't need it for emissions testing, get rid of the dang thing!  Your car will sound better and I don't think it will affect performance much.||||reg||1
